## ClangFormat spec for sparrow project, ie the edge lightweight computation
## engine's C++ code.
##
## Brief:
##   In general, we prefer using Google Cpp Style for simplicity. But we allow
##   some specification for simplicity, as following :
##   
##   1. We allow RTTI, only for dynamic_cast. This gives better runtime safety
##      during the early stage of the project. Notes, exception is still not
##      allowed
##
##   2. We use boost and many third-parties. In most cases, we don't allow direct
##      reference but instead suggesting sandbox the API to match the coding
##      convention, ie disable exception but turn them into error code.

## Notes, this is only for C++, not for JavaScript, Python and others used in
## test suites

BasedOnStyle: Google

## Some simple overrides which we relax a little bit of Google coding style


## I actually set my Vim to warn me with color vertical bar in 81 characters
ColumnLimit: 80

AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true

## Save us from aligning by ourself
AlignTrailingComments: true

AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: false

## do not sort include orders, like a paranoid
SortIncludes: false
